IsLoopHeaderModuleDoc
    Version: 1
    Language: en
    Format: STF
    Purpose: Decides whether a block is a loop header. PRIORITY is the explicit term["loop"]=1 marker set by EmitLoop during lowering; the reachability heuristic is REMOVED (it falsely detected a Branch inside an outer Loop as a header via an outer back edge). Returns map {loop, body, exit}.
    Provides: IsLoopHeader(state, b) -> res. b is a block; returns map: loop=1 with body/exit = branch ids (depending on which branch closes the loop), or loop=0/body=null/exit=null when not a loop.
    DependsOn: none (marker is read from term; Reaches is no longer used).
    Composition: Native include from modules/GenWasm/GenWasm.sir (Path: ../IsLoopHeader/IsLoopHeader.sir).
    Notes: used by EmitBlock to generate WASM loop/block structures.
